.TH "CSSTRANSFORMVALUE.ENTRIES" "3JS" "September 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSTransformValue.entries \- CSSTransformValue: entries() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]entries()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] interface returns a new \f[I]array
iterator\f[R] that yields \f[CR][index, value]\f[R] pairs for each item
in the object.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
entries()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A new iterable iterator object.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Iterating over index/value pairs
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] transform = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20)),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSScale(2, 3),
]);

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] [index, component] \f[B]of\f[R] transform.entries()) {
  console.log(index, component.toString());
}
\f[I]// 0 \(dqtranslate(10px, 20px)\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// 1 \(dqscale(2, 3)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
